<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4066" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλη</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wandering</i> or
				<i>roaming</i> without home or hope of rest, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.464
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				56
			</span></i> (pl.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεία ἄ.</span>, as etym.
			of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλήθεια</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				421b
			</span></i>; in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Mar.</u>
				45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				7.6
			</span></i> (pl.), etc.; in pl., of the blood in fever, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Flat.</u>
				8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>wandering of mind, distraction</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1285
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνοαὶ βροτῶν ἄλαι</span>
			winds <i>that keep</i> men <i>wandering</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				194
			</span></i>.</div>
